Appendix — Pitfalls (v2)
Same named store everywhere: ManagedSettingsStore("km.restrictions") in host + monitor, or your flags silently fork.
15-minute rule on every DeviceActivitySchedule; midnight-crossing windows get split into two (23:59 → 00:00).
Monitor extension RAM ≈ 6 MB — keep SharedStore thin; no JSON bombs, no images.
Union-vs-single profile: pick one token-merging rule and stick to it (v2 uses union; if you later want per-kid earned-time accounting, track playMinutesToday per profile and re-shield by removing that kid's tokens from the union).
**Guarded enforcement under .individual:** shields themselves are system-enforced; OS-hardening flags like denyAppRemovalare strongest under.child` — verify behavior on devices across the iOS versions you support and treat the Phase-5 checklist as the authoritative backup.
App Review: state clearly in review notes that this is a parental-control app on the Screen Time API; include a short demo video (authorization → Siri-on → shield → PIN-gate exit). No distribution entitlement form needed since you're not using .child mode.
